{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_delta","contentIndex":0,"delta":" the first test.","partial":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Test List\n\nTest List Created:\n**Feature**: Claim Office\n**Test File**: claim-office.spec.ts\n**Tests**: 30\n\n**Test Cases** (ordered simple -> complex):\n1. should compute premium 5 G for empty item list -- edge case: empty item list\n2. should compute base premium 100 G for a sword\n3. should compute base premium 60 G for an amulet\n4. should compute base premium 80 G for a staff\n5. should compute base premium 40 G for a potion\n6. should compute base premium 25 G per component for runes and moonstones\n7. should compute base premium 60 G for a block of 3 alike components -- building block applies\n8. should compute base premium 50 G for 2 runes -- no block applies\n9. should compute base premium 100 G for 4 runes -- no block as block requires exactly 3\n10. should apply component block only to exactly 3 alike components of same type -- different types do not form block\n11. should compute base premium 120 G for 3 runes and 3 moonstones -- two separate blocks\n12. should add 50 % risk surcharge for cursed items -- applies to base premium of cursed item only\n13. should add 30 % risk surcharge for highly enchanted items (enchantment level ≥ 5) -- applies to base premium of enchanted item only\n14. should apply cursed surcharge only to cursed sword in multi-item policy -- modifier scope per item\n15. should apply 20 % loyalty discount for long-standing customers (≥ 2 years) -- policy-wide modifier\n16. should apply 10 % initial assessment surcharge for first insurance -- applies per item regardless of customer history\n17. should apply 15 % discount on each contract after first -- policy-wide modifier\n18. should add 5 G processing fee to every premium -- added at the very end\n19. should round final premium to whole G in MHPCO's favor -- e.g. 197.5 → 198\n20. should round final payout to whole G in MHPCO's favor -- e.g. 350.5 → 350\n21. should reject quote with unknown item type and exit with error -- e.g. broomstick\n22. should reject claim with damage to item not in policy and exit with error\n23. should reject claim with negative damage amount and exit with error\n24. should compute payout 400 G for regular sword damage 500 G -- standard reimbursement minus deductible\n25. should compute payout 100 G for rune damage 200 G -- standard reimbursement minus deductible\n26. should apply 100 G deductible per damaged item -- applies once per item in damage event\n27. should cap total payout per policy at twice the insurance sum\n28. should reimburse damage to items with enchantment level ≥ 8 at 50 % of damage amount -- then apply deductible\n29. should fully reimburse damage to items made of dragon material -- then apply deductible\n30. should apply both 50 % rule and deductible for dragon-material sword with enchantment 9 -- 50 % rule wins\n31. should fully reimburse dragon-material sword with enchantment 5 -- only dragon-material clause applies\n32. should reject claim if damages array has more entries of a type than insured -- claim validation\n33. should compute premium 165 G for cursed sword by newcomer -- integration example\n34. should compute premium 160 G for cursed highly-enchanted sword by long-standing customer on second contract -- integration example, first insurance applies to new item\n35. should reduce second claim payout when cap is partially exhausted -- cap exhaustion example\n\nTest List Phase Complete. Proceeding to Red phase with the first test."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"nebius/qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-instruct-2507","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784951651285,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-b70b58f0-76ac-45b4-a51c-62bd679cb421","responseModel":"Qwen/Qwen3-